);</span>\n<span class=\"p\">}</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>currently yields:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Rust\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"cp\">$</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">cargo</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">run</span>\n<span class=\"n\">thread</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">'</span><span class=\"na\">main</span><span class=\"o\">'</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">panicked</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">at</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">..</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"o\">/</span><span class=\"n\">wasmtime</span><span class=\"o\">-</span><span class=\"mf\">50.0.0</span><span class=\"o\">/</span><span class=\"n\">src</span><span class=\"o\">/</span><span class=\"n\">runtime</span><span class=\"o\">/</span><span class=\"n\">bug</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"n\">rs</span><span class=\"p\">:</span><span class=\"mi\">63</span><span class=\"p\">:</span><span class=\"mi\">13</span><span class=\"p\">:</span>\n<span class=\"nc\">BUG</span><span class=\"p\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nc\">Instance</span><span class=\"p\">::</span><span class=\"n\">start_call</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">called</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">without</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">running</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">event</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">loop</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>If <code>call_async</code> is used, however, this works fine. This is something where the spec has changed over time where originally we could rely on normal component model traps to ensure that <code>Func::call</code> pretty much worked as expected, but with recent spec changes it effectively requires the event loop to be running and to activate fibers and such.</p>\n<p>In essence a synchronous entrypoint for component model functions is no longer really compatible with the component model spec definition. I don't know exactly how to thread this needle myself, but we may want to consider deprecating <code>Func::call</code>.</p>\n</blockquote>",
